  "id": "DrugBank_DB01172 - MONDO_4471",
  "verbalization": "Kanamycin is implicated in the pathogenesis of Bacterial Arthritis through a chain of indications that link it to bacterial infections. The evidence suggests that Kanamycin is associated with conditions like Arachnoiditis and Igg4-related Pachymeningitis, which in turn are linked to Ceftizoxime, a drug used to treat bacterial infections. This creates a pathway where Kanamycin may contribute to the development of bacterial arthritis by exacerbating or facilitating bacterial infections. The presence of multiple indications pointing to bacterial arthritis through different routes supports the hypothesis that Kanamycin could play a role in the progression of bacterial arthritis, possibly by modulating immune responses or promoting bacterial proliferation. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Kanamycin to be involved in the development of bacterial arthritis through a mechanism that involves immune-related processes and antibiotic use.",
